codex
The new stmap15 guard does not preserve the intended stmap14 behavior before the adaptive profile threshold is reached. Existing commands appear isolated, but the new command's core behavior is wrong.

Review comment:

- [P2] Preserve stmap14 fallback before profile opens — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:497-501
  When mode 16 is below the profile threshold, this early return rejects every lower-moderate middle-slack candidate before the area-saving check runs. That is stricter than the stated stmap14 fallback: candidates saving at least two inverter areas should still be eligible until the profile opens and lowers the margin to one inverter.
The new stmap15 guard does not preserve the intended stmap14 behavior before the adaptive profile threshold is reached. Existing commands appear isolated, but the new command's core behavior is wrong.

